      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe the com.android.bluetooth.flags.enable_sniff_offload aflag persists through reboots.\n\nThe sniff offload feature is controlled by a combination of the com.android.bluetooth.flags.enable_sniff_offload aflag and bluetooth.sniff_offload.enabled sysprop. I want to make sure we don\u0027t have a developer or tester change the flag + sysprop from the default value, then reboot and have the sysprop reset to default and the flag persist. That would leave the developer or tester in a broken sniff offload state.",
